    {
      "id": "3341ef1a0dd3b93ad63ac9af1f028cfbe4b980e6",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2216961815,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Is there any reason to change `samples_` below from `int` to `qsizetype`? My understanding is that `samples_` does not refer to the number of packets, but the number of samples (at minimum every 100ms by default) that have been taken. The 31-bit integer will overflow after at least six years (`2**31 / 10 / 3600 / 24 / 365 = 6.8`), I don't think there is a reason to change the type?\n\nFurthermore, the above code using `samples_` is not designed to be large values since an allocation of that size will me made:\n\nhttps://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qlist.html#QList-7\n> QList::QList(qsizetype _size_, Qt::Initialization)\n>\n> Constructs a list with an initial size of _size_ elements.\n\nhttps://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qvector.html#QVector-2\n> QVector::QVector(int _size_, const T &_value_)\n>\n> Constructs a vector with an initial size of _size_ elements. Each element is initialized with _value_.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2415432,
            "username": "Lekensteyn",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Peter Wu",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/efcf30db53f30b15e7c905ef37bd4dc44d87573bd92baf97cd707115d3fcd0c0?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/Lekensteyn"
