      "title": "capture info: Store total counts as 64 bit integers",
      "message": "capture info: Store total counts as 64 bit integers\n\nWireshark can't handle more than 2^31-1 packets in the packet list\n(because QTreeView uses an int to count the number of rows), and\ntshark can't handle more than 2^32-1 packets.\n\nHowever, dumpcap is not limited to capturing only a 32 bit number\nof packets, and if the packet list is not being updated in real time,\nand multiple files are used so that no file has too many packets to\nopen, it's possible to capture more than 2^32 packets in a single\nsession without issues. When capture stops, the last file will be\nopened, but not until then.\n\nThe capture info dialog ought to still work in such a situation.\n\ncap_session->count can be a uint64_t for the same reason (it\nonly should get that large in a \"don't update the packet list in\nreal time\" session) so that the main status bar also can handle big\nnumbers.\n\nFix #20233\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2024-11-18T10:21:39.000-05:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
      "committer_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2024-11-19T21:46:01.000+00:00",
